# Windows batch files must be checked out with CRLF: cmd.exe's parser is unreliable
# on LF-only files (goto labels and multi-line ( ) blocks are the classic casualties).
# Editors and cross-platform copies can still produce LF, so the sample bats are also
# written to survive LF: no labels, no blocks, no chaining - every line stands alone.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
